# Artboards carry a shared foundation block that check-artboards.mjs compares
# byte for byte, and the builders assert LF on their source. With core.autocrlf
# on Windows a fresh clone would hand out CRLF copies and fail both for a reason
# nothing on screen would show.
*.dc.html text eol=lf

# PDFs are binary: the manual-ingestion test fixtures (and any PDF) carry byte offsets in
# their xref tables, and an end-of-line conversion on checkout would corrupt them. A PDF
# with no NUL byte otherwise looks like text to git.
*.pdf binary
